🚽 Test case: #193 -- returning a struct-returning call result (`bussin
🚽 make(a,b);`) must execute the call exactly ONCE. A static counter inside
🚽 make() witnesses the count. Before PR #254's fix, ast_accept()'s
🚽 NODE_RETURN pre-visit ran the call (and freed its result) and then
🚽 handle_return_statement() ran it again -- printing "make called 2 times"
🚽 -- even though the returned value was still correct, so a value-only test
🚽 could not see the duplicated side effect.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
    rizz y;
};

gang Point make(rizz a, rizz b) {
    salty rizz calls = 0;
    calls = calls + 1;
    yapping("make called %d times", calls);
    gang Point p;
    p.x = a;
    p.y = b;
    bussin p;
}

gang Point relay(rizz a, rizz b) {
    bussin make(a, b);
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point r = relay(3, 4);
    yapping("%d %d", r.x, r.y);
}
